synthesis.quality_verdict:
Engineering quality is good to strong where code exists:
- closed typed errors and fail-closed refusals;
- almost no production escape hatches (zero unwrap, unsafe only in the containment FFI, each site justified);
- about 1,450 tests that use positive controls.

Build, format, lint and docs pass. All 78 test failures in the audit trace to the audit environment.

The weaknesses are:
- 25-50% of source lines are dated history comments, and some stale headers contradict the code;
- a few god modules (run.rs at 6,500 lines);
- several built-but-unwired policy features (budget exhaustion, quarantine, mutation pinning);
- confirmed defects on operator paths: Ctrl-C is inert, status conflates items, and the Linux kill bug is fixed only on the remote.

Everything is proven against fakes and Windows only.
